-- title:
--   Reducedness of all geometric fibres of the X₁(Mp) two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise extension of $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M*p))` of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that $p \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ equal to the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot\!$ (the power series `jNumQ`), the $q$-expansion of the $j$-invariant. Then for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every scheme morphism $x : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, the pullback of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) — the map to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ obtained from the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two charts $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ inside $K$ — along $x$ is a reduced scheme.
--
--   This is the statement that the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the discrete valuation ring $A$ of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ above $p$ has reduced geometric fibres, both at the generic point and at the closed point; classically it reflects the reducedness of the special fibre of the model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_p[\zeta_p]$. It feeds the analysis of sections, stalks and branch ideals of this model used in the study of the Jacobian and its reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_isReduced_pullback_modelTo_of_isAlgClosed_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

